From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 17:55:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audio do not declare the absent bluetooth module

The UML product omits the Bluetooth HAL, so its audio policy configuration
declares only the primary and remote-submix modules and the audio HAL creates
only IModule/default and IModule/r_submix. The service VINTF fragment still
declared IModule/bluetooth.

AudioFlinger waits for every declared IModule instance, so it blocked forever on
a module that is never registered. audioserver therefore never published
IAudioFlingerService, system_server blocked in AudioService.<init> ->
readUserRestrictions -> isMicrophoneMuted -> getService<IAudioFlingerService>,
and the watchdog killed the system process roughly every three and a half
minutes. One boot recorded 3523 servicemanager attempts to lazily start
android.hardware.audio.core.IModule/bluetooth and 18 runtime restarts in an
hour without ever reaching sys.boot_completed.

Comment the declaration out the same way this file already handles IModule/stub
and IModule/usb, whose comment states the rule: declare these only when the
modules are present in the configuration.
---
 audio/aidl/default/android.hardware.audio.service-aidl.xml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/audio/aidl/default/android.hardware.audio.service-aidl.xml b/audio/aidl/default/android.hardware.audio.service-aidl.xml
index fda4af68eb6682ac2378704ee3f6496f3281e646..4eb686230aa880185e7bf120641991ad56212490 100644
--- a/audio/aidl/default/android.hardware.audio.service-aidl.xml
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/android.hardware.audio.service-aidl.xml
@@ -9,11 +9,13 @@
     <version>4</version>
     <fqname>IModule/r_submix</fqname>
   </hal>
+  <!-- Uncomment when the bluetooth module is present in the configuration
   <hal format="aidl">
     <name>android.hardware.audio.core</name>
     <version>4</version>
     <fqname>IModule/bluetooth</fqname>
   </hal>
+  -->
   <hal format="aidl">
     <name>android.hardware.audio.core</name>
     <version>4</version>
